#!/bin/bash
# land-the-shop.sh — the Beauty Market becomes a shop: every product on the
# shelf, in labelled category sections, and a mark on the ones already in your
# routine.
#
# PRECONDITION: land-routine-sheet.sh (and therefore land-real-shelf.sh).
#
# FRONTEND ONLY (together-city-react). Push, and Vercel ships it.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="Seventy products, and a way through them"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"The routine is a sheet, not a settings screen"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-routine-sheet.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="89d40b5f7d1192ea3b33a6a2659eb42dc8bd7567d92a2a12ef6b09f9359d7f87"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-react/src/features/beauty/pages/Market.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/pages/Routine.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/components/ProductShot.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/shelf-is-browsable.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
Seventy products, and a way through them

The market has always been sent the whole shelf. `recommendProducts()` scores
every product, drops only what a declared sensitivity makes unsafe, sorts
matched first, and there is no cap anywhere in the path — so "show me
everything in the database" was already true and did not look it. Thirteen
products is a page you take in at a glance. Seventy is a wall, and at that size
being present stops being the same thing as being findable.

THE SEGMENTS WERE ALSO QUIETLY WRONG, which is the actual defect in here. Skin
and Hair were decided by looking for "Haircare", "Hair" or "Scalp" in the
display CATEGORY. True of the thirteen invented products it was written
against; false of the seventy real ones — "Shampoo" and "Conditioner" contain
none of those words, so the two most obvious hair products in the shop sat under
Skin, and the fifteen body products, a group that did not exist when the rule
was written, went there too. Nothing failed. The Skin tab just had a shampoo in
it. The catalogue carries `group` for exactly this and the page reads it now.

THE REFERENCE IS THE ORDINARY'S SHOP: a category row across the top, a filter /
title / sort bar, and a wide grid of large photographs with the name and price
centred underneath in small type. That layout is FOR comparison — you are
looking across eight bottles, not reading one — so the tile carries the four
things you compare on and everything else waits behind a disclosure.

WHAT THAT COST. The old card printed the matched-because chips, the biomarker
chips, the actives, the usage and the blurb, all at once, on every product. That
is the right density for thirteen and unreadable across seventy. All of it is
still here, one tap down, on the tile you are actually interested in.

"SORTED IN CATEGORIES" IS THE DEFAULT RATHER THAN A FILTER. With nothing chosen
the grid runs as labelled sections — Cleanser, Toner, Serum, Moisturiser — in
shelf order, because thirty-eight skincare products in one grid sorted by match
score is a heap. Choosing a category collapses to that section; typing a search
collapses to one run, because a heading reading "Serum" over a set of search
results is furniture.

Three controls and not a fourth: which part of you it is for, what kind of thing
it is, and a box to type a name into. Every one prints a count, because the
whole point of the change is being able to see that the shelf really is all
there.

AND A PRODUCT ALREADY IN YOUR ROUTINE SAYS SO. "✓ Routine · morning & evening"
on the tile, naming the bands rather than a bare tick — "in your routine" leaves
somebody hunting through four bands for the one it means. Without it the market
and the routine are two lists of products that do not acknowledge each other,
and the way you find out is by buying your own cleanser twice. It reads the
routine the citizen has already been given rather than re-deriving one, because
two answers to "is this in my routine" is one answer too many.

THE PICTURE FALLBACK IS NOW ONE COMPONENT. `ProductShot` walks primary →
alternate → category mark and both pages use it; the routine had its own copy,
which is two behaviours the day one of them is fixed. `key={src}` on the img is
the whole mechanism — without it React reuses the DOM node when the src changes
and a browser that has already failed on that node does not reliably re-fire
`onError`, so the walk stops after one step and looks like it works.

The `+` on each tile is a 44px target around a 26px mark, for the same reason
the photo grid's remove button is: the tap area is not the drawing.

shelf-is-browsable.test.ts pins the two silent ones — segmenting by `group` and
not by sniffing a category, and the routine flag being read from the routine.
It strips comments before it looks, because the first version failed on its own
subject matter: the header explaining that "Haircare" was the bug contains the
word "Haircare".

tsc clean, vitest green (60 files), a11y 0 at the ceiling, motion and lint at
theirs, vite build clean. Rendered at 1180.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS"
echo " The whole shelf, in category sections, with the routine"
echo " marked on it. Push, and Vercel ships it."
echo "==============================================================="
